@* Reusable book -> chapter -> verse-range picker (design-direction.md:
   "picker (top-right): dusk-glass panels" describes its mount on the World
   page; Task 14 adds a second, parchment-context mount in the reader
   header). Purely a controlled emitter: it knows nothing about scripture
   mode, /world, /read, or NavigateWorld/NavigateReader -- it only composes
   a canonical ref from the current selections and hands it to whatever
   OnApply the mounting page wired up.

   ThemeClass is the ONLY thing that differs between mounts: World.razor
   passes "picker-dusk", Reader.razor passes "picker-parchment". Markup and
   behavior stay identical -- app.css's .picker carries every rule that's
   the SAME in both contexts, reading the material/color/position specifics
   from custom properties the theme class sets (the same --header-fg-style
   inheritance .app-header + .header-parchment/.header-dusk already use),
   so no selector ever combines two classes.

   Batch M-D4, owner bug B4 (verbatim): "the chapter nav box in the top
   right of the reader is always stuck on genesis and doesn't follow the
   focus chapter." CurrentBook/CurrentChapter (both optional, default null)
   are the fix: Reader.razor is the ONLY mounting page that supplies them
   (its own _book/_chapterNum), so this component still "knows nothing
   about /world" -- World.razor's own mount leaves both null and this stays
   a plain, unsynced emitter there, byte-for-byte the pre-existing
   behavior. OnParametersSet (see below) only re-syncs the book/chapter
   dropdowns when CurrentBook/CurrentChapter actually CHANGE from what was
   last synced -- Reader.razor re-renders this component on every one of
   its OWN re-renders (a popover opening, a hover, ...), most of which
   never touch _book/_chapterNum at all, and clobbering the user's own
   in-progress verse-from/-to typing (or a book/chapter they're mid-browsing
   toward a DIFFERENT jump target) on every one of those unrelated
   re-renders would be a real, avoidable regression this guard exists to
   prevent. *@
@inject AtlasClient Atlas

<div class="picker @ThemeClass" data-testid="picker">
    <p class="picker-eyebrow">Scripture</p>

    <select class="picker-select" data-testid="picker-book" aria-label="Book"
            @bind="_bookCode" @bind:after="OnBookChanged">
        @if (_toc is not null)
        {
            @foreach (var b in _toc)
            {
                <option value="@b.Code">@b.Name</option>
            }
        }
    </select>

    <select class="picker-select" data-testid="picker-chapter" aria-label="Chapter"
            @bind="_chapterText" @bind:after="OnChapterChanged">
        <option value="">Chapter</option>
        @for (var c = 1; c <= ChapterCount; c++)
        {
            <option value="@c">@c</option>
        }
    </select>

    <input class="picker-verse" type="number" data-testid="picker-verse-from" aria-label="From verse"
           min="1" max="@MaxVerse" disabled="@(SelectedChapter is null)"
           value="@_verseFromText" @oninput="OnVerseFromInput" />
    <span class="picker-verse-sep" aria-hidden="true">&ndash;</span>
    <input class="picker-verse" type="number" data-testid="picker-verse-to" aria-label="To verse"
           min="1" max="@MaxVerse" disabled="@(SelectedChapter is null)"
           value="@_verseToText" @oninput="OnVerseToInput" />

    <button type="button" class="picker-apply" data-testid="picker-apply" @onclick="Apply">Go</button>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public EventCallback<string> OnApply { get; set; }
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string ThemeClass { get; set; } = "";

    // B4 -- see this file's own header comment. Null (World.razor's own
    // mount) means "don't sync at all," the pre-existing behavior.
    [Parameter] public string? CurrentBook { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public int? CurrentChapter { get; set; }

    private List<BookTocEntry>? _toc;
    private string _bookCode = "";
    private string _chapterText = "";
    private string _verseFromText = "";
    private string _verseToText = "";

    // B4's own "already reflects this" guard -- the LAST (book, chapter)
    // this component actually synced the dropdowns TO, distinct from
    // _bookCode/_chapterText (the user's own live selection, which OnApply
    // reads and which a book/chapter dropdown CHANGE handler mutates
    // independently of this field). Null until the first real sync.
    private (string Book, int Chapter)? _synced;

    // B4: a real, live-caught race, not a theoretical one -- found by this
    // batch's own new Playwright coverage, not guessed. Reader.razor's own
    // FIRST-ever render (mid its own OnInitializedAsync, before route
    // params have been applied) still carries _book/_chapterNum's plain
    // field-initializer defaults ("GEN"/1) -- this component's OWN first
    // SetParametersAsync call sees CurrentBook="GEN" for that one instant.
    // Blazor does NOT wait for THIS method's own in-flight Atlas.Books()
    // fetch before invoking a LATER SetParametersAsync call on the SAME
    // instance (the `_initialized` guard in ComponentBase.SetParametersAsync
    // is set synchronously, before OnInitializedAsync's await even starts,
    // so a second call always takes the "already initialized" branch
    // straight into OnParametersSet, regardless of whether this method's
    // own continuation has resolved yet) -- so Reader's OWN real, routed
    // CurrentBook/CurrentChapter ("EXO"/3) can arrive and correctly sync
    // (OnParametersSet below) WHILE this fetch is still pending. Without
    // reading CurrentBook/CurrentChapter HERE too, the unconditional
    // `_bookCode = _toc[0].Code` fallback below would then fire AFTER that
    // correct sync and silently clobber it back to "GEN" the instant this
    // await finally resolves -- confirmed live: the picker settled on "GEN"
    // even though OnParametersSet's own _synced bookkeeping believed it was
    // already showing "EXO" (CurrentBook, a shared mutable property on this
    // SAME instance, already read "EXO" by the time this continuation ran,
    // so _synced was never wrong -- only _bookCode/_chapterText were,
    // clobbered by this method AFTER OnParametersSet's own correct write).
    // Reading CurrentBook/CurrentChapter fresh here (never a value
    // captured before the await) closes the race in both possible
    // orderings: whichever of this fetch or Reader's own route-driven
    // update resolves LAST simply confirms the same already-correct sync.
    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _toc = await Atlas.Books();
        if (_toc.Count == 0)
        {
            return;
        }

        if (CurrentBook is { } book && CurrentChapter is { } chapter)
        {
            _synced = (book, chapter);
            _bookCode = book;
            _chapterText = chapter.ToString();
        }
        else
        {
            _bookCode = _toc[0].Code;
        }
    }

    // B4: runs on EVERY Reader.razor re-render (this component is an
    // unconditional child of its own mounting page), by design -- see this
    // file's own header comment for why _synced (not a bare "did the
    // parameter change" Blazor doesn't track for you) is what keeps this a
    // no-op on the overwhelming majority of those. CAN fire while _toc is
    // still null/loading (a genuine re-render of an ALREADY-initialized
    // instance never re-runs OnInitializedAsync, and can arrive before this
    // component's own FIRST OnInitializedAsync call has resolved at all --
    // see that method's own header comment for the real race this app once
    // hit) -- harmless here, since this method never reads _toc; the
    // dropdown's own options simply populate once OnInitializedAsync's
    // fetch eventually does resolve, correctly showing whatever _bookCode/
    // _chapterText already hold by then.
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
    {
        if (CurrentBook is not { } book || CurrentChapter is not { } chapter)
        {
            return; // World.razor's own mount -- stays unsynced, unchanged
        }

        if (_synced is { } prior && prior.Book == book && prior.Chapter == chapter)
        {
            return; // already reflects this exact chapter -- don't clobber in-progress typing
        }

        _synced = (book, chapter);
        _bookCode = book;
        _chapterText = chapter.ToString();
        _verseFromText = "";
        _verseToText = "";
    }

    private BookTocEntry? SelectedBookEntry => _toc?.FirstOrDefault(b => b.Code == _bookCode);
    private int ChapterCount => SelectedBookEntry?.Chapters.Count ?? 0;

    private int? SelectedChapter =>
        int.TryParse(_chapterText, out var c) && c >= 1 && c <= ChapterCount ? c : null;

    private int MaxVerse => SelectedChapter is int c ? SelectedBookEntry!.Chapters[c - 1] : 0;

    // A new book invalidates any chapter chosen against the old one (chapter
    // counts differ book to book) and, transitively, any verse range (bounded
    // by that now-stale chapter).
    private void OnBookChanged()
    {
        _chapterText = "";
        _verseFromText = "";
        _verseToText = "";
    }

    // A new chapter invalidates any verse range chosen against the old one --
    // verse bounds are per-chapter (TOC's Chapters[chapter-1]).
    private void OnChapterChanged()
    {
        _verseFromText = "";
        _verseToText = "";
    }

    private void OnVerseFromInput(ChangeEventArgs e) => _verseFromText = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "";
    private void OnVerseToInput(ChangeEventArgs e) => _verseToText = e.Value?.ToString() ?? "";

    // Composes the canonical ref per the exact CONTRACT shapes: book only
    // ("GEN"), +chapter ("GEN.1"), +verse-from alone or verse-from==verse-to
    // ("GEN.1.5"), or a strict from<to range ("GEN.1.5-9"). Each step only
    // extends the ref if the step before it is itself present and in range,
    // so a blank or out-of-bounds verse box just truncates the ref back to
    // whatever's still valid instead of composing a broken one.
    private async Task Apply()
    {
        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(_bookCode))
        {
            return;
        }

        var sref = _bookCode;
        if (SelectedChapter is int chapter)
        {
            sref = $"{sref}.{chapter}";
            if (int.TryParse(_verseFromText, out var from) && from >= 1 && from <= MaxVerse)
            {
                sref = $"{sref}.{from}";
                if (int.TryParse(_verseToText, out var to) && to > from && to <= MaxVerse)
                {
                    sref = $"{sref}-{to}";
                }
            }
        }

        await OnApply.InvokeAsync(sref);
    }
}
